sec.p:
Laboratory investigations showed a suppressed thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) level of <0.003 µIU/mL (reference range: 0.350–4.940 µIU/mL) and an elevated free thyroxine (free T4) level of >5 ng/dL (reference range: 0.70–1.48 ng/dL). Thyroid scintigraphy using technetium-99m pertechnetate revealed diffuse increased uptake consistent with toxic diffuse goiter (
Fig. 1
). Based on clinical, biochemical, and imaging findings, a diagnosis of Graves' disease-associated psychosis was established.
